Fig. S8 Representative results of PSF modeling analysis for different-sized dielectric nanoparticles ((a) Rnom = 20 
nm, (b) 50 nm, and (c) 60 nm). The RMSE map shows the representative RMSE values for the whole parameter 
space of ni and zp, trying to find the best fit (marked by a red arrow). The axial contrast profile in the middle of 
each row shows the best simulation curve (red line with dots) for each experimental curve (blue line with dots). 
The SHIP images, one by experiment (top) and one by simulation (bottom) with the best parameter values: the fit 
results (ni, zp) = (1.538, 0.022 Î¼m) for (a), (ni, zp) = (1.519, 0.039 Î¼m) for (b), and (ni, zp) = (1.515, 0.052 Î¼m) for 
(c) with design parameters (ns, np, ni*, ng*, ti*, tg*) = (1.33, 1.59, 1.52, 1.52, 100 Î¼m, 170 Î¼m), exhibit clear similarity, 
indicating the reliability of the parameters obtained here. 
 
  

